// How an agent appraises the significant events of its life. Each event has two
// kinds of effect:
//   traits  PERSISTENT shifts to innate disposition (opposed traits move the other
//           way automatically — raising vengeance lowers forgiveness).
//   moods   TRANSIENT spikes to current feeling, which then fade (see moods.ron) —
//           and a sustained feeling, in turn, slowly reshapes the matching trait.
// This is an agent's *values*: author them freely.
[
    // Tasting power feeds ambition for good, and brings a flush of joy. In achlydesa a
    // throne is one of the blind god's gifts: taking it also deepens *devotion* to the
    // order that granted it, and the joy comes shot through with the cult's manufactured
    // *rapture* — the sweeter the counterfeit, the more there is to break.
    (event: "Crowned", traits: [("ambition", 0.05), ("devotion", 0.05)], moods: [("joy", 0.7), ("rapture", 0.4)]),
    // Being cast down stirs hot anger; left to smoulder, anger is what — over a life of
    // being wronged — hardens into a lasting grudge (anger shapes vengeance). It also opens
    // a *despair* that, sustained, wears the soul toward oblivion: the wheel grinds the
    // fallen toward forgetting.
    (event: "Deposed", moods: [("anger", 0.9), ("despair", 0.5)]),
    // Crossing a line you knew was forbidden hardens you to it: the first taboo broken makes
    // the next come easier (vengeance up, and so forgiveness down). But the Law leaves its
    // residue — *guilt*, which sustained bends a soul toward submission. That is what the
    // Archons' law is *for*: not to prevent the sin, but to mark the sinner.
    (event: "Transgressed", traits: [("vengeance", 0.05)], moods: [("guilt", 0.6)]),
]
